  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine: Advancing the Sustainability of the Judicial Reform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To reinforce independent oversight of judicial selection and vetting. 2) To enhance professional skills and operational effectiveness of judges and court staff of the High Anti-Corruption Court and the Specialised High Administrative Courts. 3) To strengthen the capacity of the Service of Disciplinary Inspectors (SDI) to review complaints against sitting judges on merits professionally, transparently, and in a timely manner. 4) To ensure relevant national and international stakeholders are effectively engaged in advancing legislative measures addressing critical reforms of the Cupreme Court and the State Judicial Administration (SJA).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: The High Council of Justice (HCJ),  the High Qualification Commission of Judges  (HQCJ), the Ethics Council, the SDI, the SDI Selection Commission, the Public Council of International Experts (PCIE), the Public Integrity Council (PIC), the High Anti-Corruption Court (HACC), the Specialised High Administrative Court, the Supreme Court, the SJA, the National School of Judges, and the Government of Ukraine.Indirect beneficiaries: Ukrainian population at large.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to solidify and advance judicial reform gains in Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
